# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Datehaja — third-party secrets
#
#   cp .env.example .env      # .env is gitignored, never commit it
#   # fill in the values below
#   bun run env:push          # -> dev deployment
#   bun run env:push:prod     # -> production
#   bun run verify:prod       # makes a REAL call to each provider
#
# These live on the Convex deployment, not in your app bundle. Vite only
# exposes VITE_*-prefixed variables to the browser, and nothing here is
# prefixed, so none of it can reach the client.
#
# NOT in this file, on purpose:
#   CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT / VITE_CONVEX_URL  -> .env.local, written by `convex dev`
#   JWT_PRIVATE_KEY / JWKS / SITE_URL    -> already set, and differ per
#                                           deployment. `env:push` refuses to
#                                           touch them. See README.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ── REQUIRED ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# OpenAI — candidate ranking, venue extraction, plan writing.
# https://platform.openai.com/settings/organization/api-keys ("Create new secret key")
# New accounts are prepaid: add credit at Settings -> Billing or every call 429s.
# Without this Datehaja still works, but falls back to rule-based extraction and
# a templated plan, and labels the result "Unconfirmed details".
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# AgentMail — the Datehaja Concierge inbox that sends every email and login OTP.
# https://console.agentmail.to -> API Keys -> Create New API Key (starts `am_`,
# shown once). Free tier: 3 inboxes, 3,000 emails/month, no card.
# Without this passwordless sign-in is unavailable; non-auth sends are logged
# as `skipped_no_provider`.
AGENTMAIL_API_KEY=am_...


# ── OPTIONAL ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Firecrawl — already works WITHOUT a key. /v2/search serves unauthenticated
# requests at a lower rate limit, which is how the live deployment runs today.
# A key raises the limit and unlocks /v2/scrape (403 without one), which is used
# to deepen thin search results.
# https://firecrawl.dev -> Dashboard -> API Keys (starts `fc-`)
# FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=fc-...

# Overrides the head of the model ladder in convex/integrations/openai.ts.
# Leave unset unless you want to pin a specific model.
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5.6-terra

# Google OAuth — shown only when both values exist on a deployment.
# Redirect URI:
#   https://<your-convex-site>.convex.site/api/auth/callback/google
# AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=...
# AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=...

# Sign in with Apple for the production HTTPS deployment. The secret is
# Apple's signed client-secret JWT and must be rotated before it expires.
# Redirect URI:
#   https://<your-convex-site>.convex.site/api/auth/callback/apple
# AUTH_APPLE_ID=...
# AUTH_APPLE_SECRET=...

# ── PROVISIONED, NOT TYPED ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Don't fill these in by hand. Once AGENTMAIL_API_KEY is pushed, run:
#
#   bunx convex run --prod setup:provisionAgentMail \
#     '{"webhookUrl":"https://merry-bass-190.convex.site/webhooks/agentmail"}'
#
# It creates the Concierge inbox and its signed webhook and prints both values.
# Paste them back here and re-run `env:push:prod`, or set them directly.
#
# AGENTMAIL_INBOX_ID=datehaja-concierge@agentmail.to
# AGENTMAIL_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
